In merge_full replace the fallback with an error match:
```rust
let tree = match Tree::from_entries(merged, limits) {
    Ok(t) => t,
    // A FileDirectory conflict was already pushed above; the best-effort tree is ours.
    Err(ag_tree::TreeError::FileDirectoryConflict { .. }) => ours.clone(),
    Err(e) => return Err(e.into()),
};
```
(`merged` can be moved, the `.clone()` is not needed.) I applied this on a scratch copy: it compiles, the same repro now returns `ERR tree has too many entries (6)`, and `cargo test -p ag-merge` passes (36 tests). The callers already turn Err into Error::Invalid (integrate.rs:397-398, workspace.rs:267, virtual_ws.rs:193). Add a unit test in ag-merge/src/tests.rs using the existing helpers:
```rust
#[test]
fn union_over_tree_limit_is_an_error_not_a_clean_merge() {
    let io = Mem::default();
    let base = tree(&io, &[("a","1"),("b","1")]);
    let ours = tree(&io, &[("a","1"),("b","1"),("o1","x"),("o2","x")]);
    let theirs = tree(&io, &[("a","1"),("b","1"),("t1","y"),("t2","y")]);
    let tight = Limits { max_tree_entries: 4, ..Limits::default() };
    assert!(merge_trees(&base, &ours, &theirs, &io, &tight).is_err());
}
```

```rust
let tree = match ours.apply(&ops, limits) {
    Ok(t) => t,
    // merge_full reports file/directory collisions as FileDirectory conflicts.
    Err(ag_tree::TreeError::FileDirectoryConflict { .. }) => return Ok(None),
    Err(e) => return Err(e.into()),
};
```
This compiles (TreeError converts into IoError via `?`/`.into()`) and ag-merge's 36 tests still pass, including the strategies_agree proptest. Ship it together with the finding-0 fix and its limit test. Optionally add `debug_assert!(!matches!(e, TreeError::NoOpPut(_) | TreeError::DeleteMissing(_)))` in the Err(e) arm.

